A||||41||rogergarrison||Mitsubishi 3000 GT||||1||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||03-20-2001||01:18 PM||||Well after years, I finally got to drive a dealers 3000GT. I immeadiatly come to the conclusion that its emmense power is media hype. Although it is sporty, its performance doesnt impress me at all. Id save my money and buy the Dodge Stealth for half the money and use the differnce to buy a bunch of new toys. I would have no problem blowing this car away with my Fiero kitcar. I dont know about top speed but the 160 mph speedo seems a little bit of a fantasy, really pretty lame for a dbl overhead cam, 4 valve cyl, V6.<P>also got to drive a Subaru SVX. It also is dbl OHC, 4 valve V6. Much more power, lots quicker. Parts are all pretty cheezy though. Most of the interior was falling apart although it does look pretty cool. Both were here for some minor touch up work with fresh dealer tune ups. Ive never seen this one before. Its a sports coupe in same class as 3000GT, Supra, 300Z.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||03-20-2001||01:39 PM||||The SVX is sweet.  They didn't sell to good so Subaru stopped making them.  I think the last year they barely sold 1100.  <P>What did you think about the handling of the SVX?  Did you really push it?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ferg||03-20-2001||01:40 PM||||Did you test drive the twin turbo 3000? A friend of mine had a base model stealth and it was pretty quick w/ 5 spd. <P>I liked the 3000 over the stealth b/c of the rear wing. The stealth blocked my rear visibility and that bugged me.<P>I've heard the twin turbo AWD stealth's were awesome on the roads. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||03-20-2001||02:14 PM||||this 3000 is non turboed, Im sure that would make a differnce. Also seems very squirly weaving it around.<P>The SVX was more stable, dont know if there AWD or not. Lots more acceleration. I liked the inside lookswise-very Ferrari like. The small numbers must be why Ive never seen one before. Youd have to get used to the bar running thru the window glass, like a Lambo.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||03-20-2001||02:19 PM||||Friend of mine in metro Denver clocked a quarter mile 13.51@100.37 MPH last year with his twin-turbo 3000GT in Denver, even with deliberately letting off the throttle while shifting. (letting off closes the throttle plate and the turbos spin down a bit, but it doesn't shift anywhere as hard.)  That was before he'd upgraded the turbos.<P>(For you Denverites it was at Bandimere Speedway, altitude is ~ 5600', measured barometric pressure was 26.xx at the time)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||03-20-2001||03:03 PM||||I've seen 135-140 in a non turbo Stealth(93 es) outside of atlanta, saw it from the backseat of the Stealth. my brother was playing with some other cars.. too bad didn't see any Fiero's on that trip.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||p4n1c||03-20-2001||03:23 PM||||I've been in a Stealth doing 240kph(150mph)  This was a base model 5-spd.  There was no rocking or swaying at that speed, we were going down the 407 here in Toronto.  They are quick for the weight of them, but the handling leaves something to be desired.  This was a '92 Stealth, 3.0 V6 I beleive.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||03-20-2001||03:45 PM||||SVX are AWD.  they only sold 1100 of them because the yen went to hell and the price of hte car went from $25,000 to $44,000 in 4 years! (Roger, Lisa told me that you had a SVX there, you need to let her drive that thing... they are sweet cars, ride well and feel very solid.  the interior is feels like a cockpit, like the fiero)<P>as for the 3000 Gt, did you drive the AWD/AWS car (i believe its the vr4)?  a friend has one, and had been nagging me to take it for a spin.  so we hop in it, take off and enter this long sweeping right hander at 100 mph... came out of it at 75!  that car scared the shiite out of me.  it was deliberatly trying to understeer (or it felt that way).  the all wheel steering moves the rear wheels in the same direction as the front.  like this:<P>/ /  or \ \<P>whereas the Honda system that they had on the prelude moves the rears in the oposite direction as the front:  / \ or \ /  which makes more sense from a perfomrance standpoint.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||03-20-2001||04:01 PM||||hoop, I think this is prob a base 3000, but the SVX def impressed me much more. The general info here tells me Im right about preferring the stealth to the 3000. Were talking at least $20K differnce. That can buy a ton of go-fast stuff.  Maybe one of these days theyll have a turbo version to update my opinion. I generally dont take other peoples say so - I say 'show me the money' first hand.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||bHooper||03-20-2001||04:45 PM||||i cant remember, i think the vr4 3000 is a turbo (where's travis when you need him?).<P>besides its a moot point... both cars have now gone the way of the fiero, rx7 and 300z... the corporate funeral pyre!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000010||danny boy||03-20-2001||05:28 PM|||| 3000GT/Stealth non turbo cars are slow.<BR>       222HP + 3900# car + SLOW<BR> If it was a base then its even less than that.<P>Drive a twinturbo.14.0 sec qtr mile stock. Add a few goodies and your in the 11/12s.<BR> For as heavy as they are they handle very well.The thing I don't care for the AWS, feels like the early Fiero bumpsteer. Not Supra or 300ZX well, but well. I smoke C5 corvettes in mine. <BR>I've yet to get a 1/4 mile run in with the new turbos/injectors/boost controller/downpipe/exaust, but last year on my first track experience ever the car was stock and I ran a 14.53 even missing second gear.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||bHooper||03-20-2001||08:35 PM||||oh yeah, did i mention how incredibly unballanced these cars are?  my friend caused this idiot to spin off (no contact, all braking)of the track (at vir), doing touring laps, last fall.  ||||reg||13
Z||000012||2M4ever||03-22-2001||01:33 AM||||As a faithful Fiero owner and a Stealth Turbo owner I can honestly say they're amazing cars.  All Wheel Drive, All Wheel Steering, Active Suspension, Twin Turbocharged, Twin Intercooled, all sorts of other goodies.  A tad heavy but more than enough power to make up for it plus with a little tweaking you can squeez 400hp out for very little money.  I know I have||||reg||1
