Z||000015||RS VR-4||03-22-2001||02:31 AM||||As an owner of both cars, 86 gt and 95 vr-4, and a previous owner of a 92 base stealth, I can say that a base stealth and a fiero gt are pretty evenly matched.  The stealth has 160 hp and weighs around 3100 lbs.  The fiero has 140 and weighs around 2800 lbs.  So acceleration is close but I would say that the fiero handles a little better.  As far as my vr-4 goes, I cant even compare the two,  acceleration or handling, the vr-4 is incredible.<BR>Later<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000016||GT Bastard||03-22-2001||09:30 AM||||I played around with a 3000GT VR4 in my Possessed '86SE 4sp that 1FST2M6 modded to hell.  He pulled up along side and gave the rev, so I dropped it into second gear and smashed the gas.  He did the same and for a split second I thought I was pulling away from him.  Then he proceeded to spank me like a little girl.  Afterwords he claimed it was a 12second car... I believe it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||03-22-2001||10:21 AM||||We have had a few come out to shannonville and mosport , Great cars in a straight line , but the weight kills them in the corner. One of the guys in our club had one , and was building it for the one lap of america (he has won it twice) car was fast in a straight line , technology , but he could turn faster lap times in his 72 Datsun 240 street car (it ran 13.8's) , the 3000 was awd , full loaded , gutted out and it was still heavy , slid a lot when pushed and became a handful to drive , he scrapped the project and sold the car. However he said it was a great highway car.<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000018||i_luv_TTs||03-22-2001||10:33 AM||||(like the bit of sexual innuendo in my username? LOL)<P>Anyone in Northern Indiana, near South Bend who would like to take a ride or even race a Stealth TT (pretty much stock), reply here because I'd be more than willing to show you what they can do.<P>rogergarrison, the "emmense power" in the media is for the VR4 version, you drove a non-turbo version. Drive a VR4 or Stealth TT and see what you think.<P>I also autocross my car and am very competitive in my division (A-Stock). I've also beat several SuperStock cars. So while it is a bit heavy in corners, it's made up by the AWD and accelleration. I regularly beat 85 and older Corvettes, also beat all the F-Bodies and am very competitive with many older Porches. <P>As for top speeds, I know a guy that had his TT up to 207 MPH (that's based on RPM and gearing calculations because the speedos aren't accurate). He was slightly modded with a turbo controller. My car has been up to 185 and then I chickened out.<P>As for Fieros, I don't want to come on here and bash... they are cool looking cars but the power just isn't there. And safety-wise, you'd never find me riding/driving one. I had a friend who lost control on an icy road, spun into the other lane and was hit by a full-size Ford F150. Estimated speed 15 mph for the truck and 10mph for the Fiero... my friend was instantly decapitated.<P>So in the safety arena, 3000GTs and Stealths are far superior. I've read several stories, seen several pictures of walk-away accidents where the car took all the damage, etc.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000019||Black88GT||03-22-2001||11:06 AM||||Oh please, decapitated? 185?  <P>   <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/bullshit.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Greg Piet||03-22-2001||11:13 AM||||Just for the record, the Fiero is an immensely safe vehicle!  Go see its crash test results!  I cannot argue about the power though.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by i_luv_TTs:<BR><B>As for Fieros, I don't want to come on here and bash... they are cool looking cars but the power just isn't there. And safety-wise, you'd never find me riding/driving one. I had a friend who lost control on an icy road, spun into the other lane and was hit by a full-size Ford F150. Estimated speed 15 mph for the truck and 10mph for the Fiero... my friend was instantly decapitated.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">  <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000021||i_luv_TTs||03-22-2001||11:20 AM||||You know, SCREW YOU *******  black88gt!<P>Yes, DECAPITATED. The truck's front bumper came thru the driver's door by about 2.5  feet, the bumper hit her head and the force decapitated her. You want her parents phone number so they can describe it to you in gruesome details?<P>And why would you think 185 in a 308 HP sports car would be bullshit? The car was still pulling, too... but I was on a back road and it was getting dark so I decided that was enough. I regularly have my car to 130-140 (probably 2-3 times a week). 185 is pretty common in a TT.<P>1st gear 0-40, 2nd gear 40-80, 3rd gear 80-120, 4th gear 120-160, 5th gear 160 to ???.<P>I also had a lot of fun once following a Ferarri thru the back roads at 150-160 mph, when we stopped he gave me a ton of kudos for keeping up. Oh, and it was a REAL Ferarri.<P>Ya know, I don't mind Fieros except for the safety issue. I said they are pretty cool cars. But *******  owners like you are what give the cars a bad name. <P>How much $$ do you have to put into YOUR car to get it to do 11.5 1/4 miles??<P>||||reg||1
