Z||000023||i_luv_TTs||03-22-2001||11:40 AM||||Ok, I did find some crash tests results:<P>from <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nhtsa.dot.gov</A> <P>Tested car: 1993 Dodge Stealth 2-DR. HB<BR>(that's basically the same car as mine, the only Stealth they tested)<P>Drivers side FIVE STARS<P>Weight 3269 pounds (weight is a big factor in safety, heavier the better)<P>Below, the lower the number the better:<P>Driver's Side Head 273hic <BR>Chest:45 g <BR>Femur: Left 1055 lb Right 1215 lb <BR>Passenger's Side Head: 985hic <BR>Chest: 41 g <BR>Femur: Left 2003 lb Right 1257 lb<P>----------<P>I didn't find any results for the Fiero in either NHTSA or the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety. But it's a much ligher and lower to the ground car so logic would say it's less safe.<P> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||i_luv_TTs||03-22-2001||11:45 AM||||black88Gt, again SCREW YOU.<BR>I have several witnesses to the Ferarri cruise. Never said it was a race. <P>What's your problem, really? I know with your piddly little 140 horsepower POS you can get envious of real cars like 3000GT VR4s and Stealth TTs but bottom line is my posts are more than believable if you knew anything about our cars.<P>Oh and no I've never seen a McClaren.<P>How much $$ do you have to put into your car to get 11.5 quarter miles? Oh, or is it even possible without dropping a big block into it? LOL<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Oreif||03-22-2001||12:40 PM||||I do not know much about the stealth/3000GT/VR4 cars. I know that some versions have gobs of power. I am only replying to the safety aspect. The Fiero was the second safest car next to a volvo during it's production years. The person you knew who was killed, was either not wearing a seatbelt or it was an accident that no matter what she was driving, she would have died. it sounds like the truck had a very high lift kit from your previous description. My Fiero is lowered and the bumper of a friends 77 Ford pick-up would hit me in the side. It is 34" to the top of the door on a stock Fiero and 36" on my 2001 Galant. The bumper of the truck had to be closer to 40" high. Any stock vehicle would have crumpled the drivers head in the accident you describe. We have a local club member who was T-boned by a full size chevy pick-up at 45mph. He basically walked away from it with a fractured rib and some minor scrapes. The link is his story including pics.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html</A> <P>There are many documented accidents involving Fiero's and the lives saved due to the chassis design. If you do a search here for "Anthony Barber" you will find a story about his accident in Colorado. His and 4 other cars were rammed head on by a kid driving a full size suburban at +75mph. Although he did sustain some serious injuries, He is alive today. When you find the thread, look at the car. You would swear the driver was killed. There was 1 person killed but he was not in a Fiero and he was the initial person hit by the truck. Most people do not understand that the plastic panels that make up the Fiero body are for looks. It is (still!) the only car where you can remove all plastic panels and the car can legally be driven. Other vehicles use the body to aid in crumple zones and strengthen the chassis. <BR>The Fiero is not an unsafe vehicle.<P>As for 3000GT's, I have a question. I saw a white 3000GT once that had the rear wing that appeared to move with the accellerator pedal or speed. It looked weird (but kind of cool) seeing the wing angle like that. Was it a special edition or an aftermarket add-on? If you know how exactly was it hooked up?<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||i_luv_TTs||03-22-2001||12:45 PM||||Ok, I don't wanna argue about safety... both of us can bring up "personal" examples, etc. so it's a moot point. <P>Let's just call it a truce on that angle.<P>As for the moving spoiler, that's a standard feature in VR4's, called "Active Aero". It is automatic based on speed it moves to create downforce. There's also a switch inside to do it manually for "waving" at chicks or whatever.<P>That feature was only on the 3000GT VR4 (twin turbo) version. The Stealth TT and VR4 had other neat features like adjustable suspension (tour/sport and in emergency maneuvers the car automatically stiffens the suspension even more to help you keep control). Also All Wheel Steering, and advanced climate control, etc. These cars are actually "GT" cars.. fast and sporty yet comfortable to drive long distances.<p>[This message has been edited by i_luv_TTs (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||Formula||03-22-2001||12:56 PM||||oh geeeeeeeeeeezzzzzzzzeeeeeeee....lol<P>ok<P>1st, the fiero isnt in the same class as a twinturbo stealth aka 3000gt aka GTO. I would take a stealth over a fiero anyday (except some of archies lol).  look at the prices when new...30k to 13k...who do you think would win lol.<P>2nd, the stealth is a little bit too big for my tastes, I know it compensates for the weight with awd and everything, but its rather large. if you like big luxary super cars then I'm fine with that, I do like stealths better then thunderbirds, monte carlos etc... But I kind of like being able to say I have a Viper Red 2 Seat Mid-Engine Sports Car!!!<P>3rd, Your comparing a 300 hp factory semi-super car to a 130 hp economy built sporty car.......????<P>4th, for the price of a stealth with low miles, all of the upgrade kits, and insurance, Im pretty sure you could have a fiero looking cool and having a reasonable amount of hp, not using a bigblock either.<P>5th, they really arent comparable so this is getting dumb lol.<P>6th Im sure someone has died in a stealth before too, it depends a lot on the type of crash, and if the driver is wearing his/her seatbelt....it sounds like being decapatitated would be unavoidable in that situation.  Im sure that the lowness of the fiero didnt help your friend but sometimes bad things happen and its not the cars fault. she might have died in a stealth too, no one will ever know, so drop it.<P>I would have more respect for someone who built an 11 sec fiero then someone who built an 11 sec sealth, The stealth would take a lot of time and money, but the fiero would need an almost complete overhaul.<P>verdict: If you have the money, can afford the parts, and like big cars, get a stealth TT.<P>If you are on a budget, like cheap mods, like to fix stuff yourself, like little cars, buy a fiero.<P>personally if I had the money I would get a stealth, but I would wreck so I'll just stick with the fiero!!<P>thank you.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yellowtored3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||rogergarrison||03-22-2001||03:03 PM||||wow didnt know Id start a war. I dont like any Japanese cars as a rule. I actually pay so little attention to them I didnt know there were diff versions. I just thought the 3000 GT was it. The one I drove was slower than my minivan. When and if I ever try a turbo one maybe ill change my opinion. As for safety, only other car to have a built in roll bar from the factory was the Avanti. And a battle with a large PU or SUV always results in a left over pile of junk, no matter what it is. Now im going to go get my boots so I can watch a 3000 go 200mph. and my Fiero drives over water.||||reg||1
Z||000029||1FST2M6||03-22-2001||03:08 PM||||uum ok.. 207.. 185.. maybe kph... NOT MPH.. the stock vicous diffs fail above 430hp... having 5-6 that come to the shop and KNOWing that there are EASY ways to make them pull 11s and being SPANKED by them on the track.. and seeing them die. the Hp needed to move a car into the 200+ range is well over 550lbft/hp Hennessey, Startech and a HOST of other tuning gurus haven't been able to break 197 in the car. RennTech of Jacksonville has a 4w Dyno and the shop has offered to pay for 2 customers that claim they can lay down more than 500hp.. ok if you can we'll pay for your hotel room AND your dyno run which is $200!  neither made over 440... and both had destroyed stock diffs and replaced them (at the shop) with KAAZ LSDs. both cars run 1.5-1.8 60' times and run high 11s.   having to drop more than $6000 in just DIffs and installation there are VERY few people that are putting enough HP/TQ to the ground to realize 170 let alone 185+ it's NOT a linear curve.. you can't just change boost and get 60hp-go faster... you have to change the turbo to support it at high loads, for a long time and have the bottom end built for it have a tranny that'll take the torque and the stress of a high speed run... for about $50k in hop-ups yeah you could have a car that'll run 200... there aren't many that have that cash. and even fewer willing to pony that up for an heavy vehicle like a stealth/3000gt/GTO even the SLs on nitrous will run 13s... but ya know what.. so did my POS Fiero! it'd go 143 pacing my Alfa... <P>At the shop right now is one of the Crown jewles.. a S/C GSR he's makin gmore than 250hp at the wheels running high 12s a daily driver and have 20k in his motor alone.. and on ONE high speed run down Ga 400 at 140 his pistons seized to the block! there are WAY to many different variable in high speed than there are in drag racing... fluid dynamics(air on the car, the fluids in the emgine and the pistons as they deteriorate in the sustained 1200+ EGTs), wind resistance <P>sorry. i'm done.. just my $.02<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||danny boy||03-22-2001||04:20 PM||||Roger, I started this. I knew there ws some Fiero owners not here that I see on the 3KGT board. Figured if I got them over here it would accomplish two things. 1) get more people aware of our board, and 2)Get some feedback from guys who have both and compare.<P>They also pointed out that I misquoted the weight of the non turbo cars. the correct weight is 3200-3300 depending on model. My car weighs 3960# with me in it.<P>1FST2M6, I  have firsthand  experience with that exploding diff thing.  Where did those guys get the Kazz diffs? I've been looking for them.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
