Z||000036||Pontiaddict||03-25-2001||12:01 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/safety.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/safety.html</A> <P>The Fiero’s results were: <BR>driver<BR>HIC -309<BR>Chest - 31 g<BR>Femur: Left  - 850 lbs : right - 840 lbs<P>passenger<BR>HIC - 356<BR>Chest - 30 g<BR>Left femur- 740 lbs<BR>right femur - 800 lbs<P>The HIC and chest ratings were the lowest at the time. The Fiero has is a slightly worse rating for head injury, (Does your Stealth have an airbag?) to the driver at least. I wouldn't want to be a passenger in your car if there was an accident, though. Not ragging on you here, I'm just giving you the info you couldn't find.||||reg||1
